Make the fidl crate visible to the overlay's own driver packages (milestone M10).

Upstream Bazel limits it to the packages listed (its examples, src, sdk/lib, ...), which
regen.py maps under //vendor/fuchsia; GN makes it visible everywhere (`//*`, the
@bazel2gn comment). A driver ported out of tree names it directly as its BUILD.gn does
(pilot 1's src/lib.rs uses fidl::endpoints), so //drivers is added. The added line is
the overlay's (Apache-2.0); the context lines are Fuchsia's (BSD-2-Clause,
LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause.txt). Applied by scripts/regen.py after patch 0001.

--- a/src/lib/fidl/rust/fidl/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/src/lib/fidl/rust/fidl/BUILD.bazel
@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@
         "//vendor/fuchsia/src:__subpackages__",
         "//vendor/fuchsia/third_party/tcpdump/tests:__subpackages__",
         "//vendor/fuchsia/tools:__subpackages__",
+        # Overlay: the overlay's driver packages (patch 0002).
+        "//drivers:__subpackages__",
     ],  # @bazel2gn:raw_overwrite:[ "//*" ]
     deps = [
         "//vendor/fuchsia/sdk/rust/zx-status",
